REQUIRED DOCUMENTS SUBMISSION: The following documents have been submitted and reviewed
by Staff:
●
Master Application; Preliminary Plat Map; Environmental Impact Assessment; Transportation
Network Plan; Open Space Narrative; Conceptual Drainage Analysis; Traffic Impact Study
●
Traffic Study Letter – submitted May 19, 2020 (submitted to update the Traffic Impact Study)
●
Response to Comments Letter; Revised Preliminary Plat Map – submitted June 15, 2020
(submitted in response to Staff Comments)

FEES DUE AT SIGNING OF THE PLAT: $12,320.00

PLANNING COMMISSION RECOMMENDATION: At their regular meeting on July 6, 2020, the City of
Cheyenne Planning Commission recommended granting an exception to UDC 4.3.3.a for block size for
Blocks 3, 4, and 7; approving single-tier lots adjacent to Van Buren Avenue for Blocks 3 and 6; and
approval of the Preliminary Plat, by a vote of 3-0, subject to the following conditions:
1. Concurrent with final plat submittal:
a. Submit a drainage study
b. Update the traffic study to address staff-requested corrections
c. Provide a narrative clarifying the relationship of the Open Space parcel Lot 20, Block 7
and the extension of James Drive on the Network Plan or Final Plat with the Final Plat
submittal.
2. On the face of subsequent final plats:
a. Place a note on applicable plats limiting access to all lots along Van Buren Avenue.
3. Prior to approval of the final plat(s), the applicant/developer shall enter into an agreement with
the City regarding impacts to Cheyenne Fire Rescue. The agreement shall identify the
applicant/developer’s proportionate share of the cost of extending service (land, facilities, and
equipment) to the area and shall be determined based on the ISO Fire Suppression Rating
Criteria and evaluation of said criteria.
4. Prior to Engineering Plan Review approval, the applicant/developer shall enter into an agreement
with the City regarding design and construction of roadway improvements (such as traffic signals,
curbs, gutter, pavement, additional lanes, traffic calming devices, etc.).  The applicant/developer
shall pay their proportionate share of costs for design and improvements based on their impact
to the system as identified in the Traffic Study submitted with this plat.
